[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, I just got done making a video on the best new features of WLED version 16 as it relates to LED strips you can check out. But, today we\'ll be looking at the biggest additions to the updated software when it comes to matrix panels, and this one you\'re not going to want to miss. Now, I did recently make a 50 by'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '50 matrix, and that turned out incredible. And I recorded every step and made a dedicated video on the project, and I\'ll leave a link to that in the description in case you\'re wanting to try something similar. But, everything I\'m about to go over can also be done on just your regular 16 by 16'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'panel or any of the other sized options out there. All right. So, to kick things off, I want to first go over the new PS matrix effects, and PS stands for particle system. These are absolutely incredible and something I hope everyone'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gets a chance to play around with themselves. PS ball pit\'s one of my favorites, and they nailed the gravity and inertia with this one. The balls are bouncing and deflecting off one another in a very realistic way that makes this so fun to watch. And with all the new PS'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'effects, there\'s about four or five different sliders that you can use to completely change the behavior and speed of the animations. Box is another fun one where the lights'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all move as if the surface is being tilted in different directions. Now, the new fire effect is one you have'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to check out because this is about as realistic as you can possibly get using LEDs. And then with the sliders, you can adjust the intensity of the flames, the flame height, and you can even introduce wind into the'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'effect, which is incredibly cool. And then the bottom slider gives you the option to reduce the size of the fire in case you don\'t want a blazing inferno. Impact is another one you definitely'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'need to check out. And the reason why I think I like it so much is because the exploding lights reminds me of when programs get de-resed in the grid. This effect also does a good job of showcasing just how far WLED has come because here you can see that the colors'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'exploding are able to push away the previous color particles. This type of spatial recognition is a huge leap forward and something you see in a lot of these new PS animations. Next is volcano and this one\'s'

[02:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'definitely in my top five. You can adjust the intensity of the lava shooting up. You can adjust the movement left and right as well as a few other controls. And keep in mind with all these effects you can of course go back and choose'

[02:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whatever color palette you want. And what might be my favorite of them all is the waterfall. And if this matrix panel was set up in my main living room area, I\'d for sure have this running at night with some water sound effects playing in the background to create an'

[02:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'epic atmosphere. And just a heads up, I did record examples of every single new PS effect included with V16 and those will be part of the final results in case you\'re'

[02:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'interested in seeing them all. But for the sake of time, let\'s move on. So I could probably do a full-length video on just the new sound react animations because they\'re that good. And if you don\'t have a keyboard, I highly recommend getting one and I promise you'

[03:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everyone in your family\'s going to want a turn. Moving on, the next big addition I\'ll go'

[03:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'over is found in Pixel Forge, other tools, and Pixel Paint. Go ahead and install and then open. This will let you paint your LED wall like it was a canvas and I won\'t spend too much time on this, but if you\'re into creating your own pixel art, this is definitely where you'

[03:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'want to go. You also get a new scrolling text program that\'s super easy to use. Put in the text you want, you can adjust the speed, size, position, and a few other'

[04:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'attributes. Then when you\'re in effects, if you choose scrolling text, whatever you put in the text program will be displayed. Now they do have a custom font builder'

[04:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that lets you upload TFT and other file types to create your own fonts that can then be used in the scrolling text program. So if you\'re wanting more variety, keep this in mind. Next, I\'ll go over what might be the coolest addition, which is the image'

[04:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tool. And this lets you upload GIFs to your matrix panel. You\'ll first want to go and download some of your favorite GIFs from the internet. I want to try the classic Homer going in the bushes. I found a couple video game ones, a rocket ship, and a few others.'

[04:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Back on the image tool, I\'ll click right here and find the one I want to upload. I\'ll first try the N64 logo. You can resize it to make sure it fits, but when it looks good, hit convert and upload a WLED.'

[04:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then at the top, you\'ll see the GIF you just uploaded. Click on it and it\'ll start playing. And this has to be about as easy as it could possibly get and definitely one of my favorite new features of V16. I\'ll play a few more of'

[05:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the other ones I found so you can see them in action. Moving on, true segment layering is'

[05:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'another awesome addition. Here I\'m going to put the lights on a basic color twinkle effect, go into segments, and then turn off the lights. Now click on add segment and this will be creating a duplicate of all of our LEDs. And for this layer, I\'m going to set the'

[05:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'animation of the PS fire effect. And then when I turn on both segments, I have everything running at once. There\'s a lot of different layering options you can choose from, but the idea is that this will let you get pretty creative in coming up with some cool designs.'

[05:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Next, I did want to mention that if this big matrix panel with 2,500 LEDs is something that you\'ll never see yourself making, I did want to quickly bring out my small 32 by 32 panel, which I made by connecting four 16 by 16 grids together.'

[05:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m using the same Glidopto controller that I use for the big project, but these LEDs are 5 V, so I\'ll be using my 5 V supply. Now, with only a little over 1,000 LEDs, I\'m able to get a very smooth 43 frames per second, and you can'

[06:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tell the difference, especially on the ball pit effect. to say that the animations look bad on the big matrix, where on average, I\'m still getting an impressive 34 frames per second, but I hope you\'re able to at least see how it'

[06:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'does look a little bit smoother on the small setup. Well, that about does it for this one, but overall, version 16 really does feel like a giant leap, and I hope you enjoyed seeing a few of the many improvements that were made when it comes to matrix panels. I\'ll leave you'

[06:34] [scene:talk]
